          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            The Adams operations have an explicit definition in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-ring"} Lambda-ring
            structure on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DefinitionInTermsOfLambdaRing"}
            below. While explicit, this definition may look contrived on first sight. But it turns out that it satisfies a list of properties, of which two simple ones already uniquely characterize the Adams operations. This is proposition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheBasicProperties"}
            below.
          #LambdaRingStructureOnKTheory.num_prop
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Lambda-ring structure on topological K-theory)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
              and write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [E] \in K(X)
              for its class in K-theory. Given
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi k
                    %mi X
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda_t[E]
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\underoverset{k = 0}{\infty}{\sum}
                    [\Lambda^k X E] t^k
                    \\;\;\in\;\;
                    K(X)[ [t] ]
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in the ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
              being the K-theory classes of the exterior powers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi k
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^k X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %p
              Since the constant term of this power series is always the unit
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mn 0
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Lambda^0 E] = 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda_t[E] \in 1 + (t) \cdot K(X)[ [t] ],
            %p
              there exists a multiplicative inverse formal power series
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi E
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_t[E]^{-1}
            %p
              Then given the class of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+vector+bundle"} virtual vector bundle
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [E] - [F] \in K(X)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi E
                    %mo −
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi F
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda_t[[E- F]]
                    \\;\;\coloneqq\;\,
                    \\lambda_t[E] \cdot \lambda_t[F]^{-1}
                    \\;\;\in\;\;
                    K(X)[ [t] ]
                    \\,.
          #DefinitionInTermsOfLambdaRing.num_prop
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (explicit definition of Adams operation)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              over some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi rank
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\psi^0(E) \coloneqq rank(E)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
              which over each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+bundle"} trivial
              vector bundle of the same
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} rank
              as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              over that component.
            %p
              Define a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in the K-theory ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ψ
                              %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %munderover
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo =
                                %mn 0
                              %mn ∞
                            %msup
                              %mi ψ
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mi t
                              %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %msup
                              %mi ψ
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mfrac
                              %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mi d
                                %mi t
                            %mi log
                            %msub
                              %mi λ
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo ∈
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\psi_t(E)
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\underoverset{k = 0}{\infty}{\sum}
                    \\psi^k(E) t^k
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\psi^0(E)
                    \-
                    t \frac{d}{d t} log \lambda_{-t}(E)
                    \\;\;\in\;\;
                    K(X)[ [t] ]
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_t
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-ring"} Lambda-ring
              operation from def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LambdaRingStructureOnKTheory"}
            %p
              Here the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithm"} logarithm
              of formal power series stands for the usual expression in terms of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+series"} geometric series
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mfrac
                              %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mi d
                                %mi t
                            %mi log
                            %msub
                              %mi λ
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi λ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mi t
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mfrac
                              %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mi d
                                %mi t
                            %msub
                              %mi λ
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munderover
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo =
                                %mn 0
                              %mn ∞
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo −
                                %msub
                                  %mi λ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mi t
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo )
                              %mi k
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mfrac
                              %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mi d
                                %mi t
                            %msub
                              %mi λ
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\frac{d}{d t} log \lambda_{-t}(E)
                    \&amp; =
                    \\frac{1}{\lambda_{-t}(E)}
                    \\frac{d}{d t}
                    \\lambda_{-t}(E)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\underoverset{k = 0}{\infty}{\sum}
                    \\left(
                    1  - \lambda_{-t}(E)
                    \\right)^k
                    \\cdot
                    \\frac{d}{d t} \lambda_{-t}(E)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                th Adams operation
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+operation"} cohomology operation
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\psi^k \;\colon\; K(-) \longrightarrow K(-)
            %p
              which is the coefficient of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t^k
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_t
          #TheBasicProperties.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (basic properties and characterization of Adams operations)
            %p The Adams operations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\psi^k \;\colon\; K(X) \longrightarrow K(X)
            %p
              have the following properties, for all elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in K(X)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mi l
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k, l \in \mathbb{N}
              and
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mtext prime
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \; \text{prime}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^k(x + y) = \psi^k(x) + \psi^k(y)
                %p
                  (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^k
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtext a line
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \,\text{a line} \;\;\Rightarrow\;\; \psi^k(x) = x^k
                %p
                  (applied to a class
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \coloneqq [L]
                  represented by a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^k
                  is the
                  = succeed "th" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+power"} tensor power
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^k(x \cdot y) = \psi^k(x) \cdot \psi^k(y)
                %p
                  (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^k
                  is in fact a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi l
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mi l
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^k(\psi^l(x)) = \psi^{k l}(x)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtext mod
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^p(x) = x^p \, \text{mod}\, p
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mover
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \tilde K(S^{2n})
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cohomology"}> reduced cohomology
                  ) then
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mover
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi k
                          %mi n
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \tilde K(S^{2n}) \hookrightarrow K(S^{2n}) \;\;\Rightarrow\;\;\psi^k(x) = k^n \cdot x
                  \.
            %p Moreover, the first two of these already uniquely characterize the Adams operations.
          %p
            For a proof see e.g.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Wirthmuller12"} Wirthmuller 12, section 11
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi k
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^n (E \oplus F) \cong \bigoplus_{k = 0}^n \Lambda^k E \otimes \Lambda^{n-k} F
          %p hence a calculation gives
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_t(x + y) = \lambda_t(x) \cdot \lambda_t(y)
          %p and thus
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi log
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log \lambda_t(x + y) = \lambda_t(x) + \lambda_t(y).
          %p
            That is,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi log
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log \lambda_t(x)
            is additive as a function of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rank
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi t
                  %mfrac
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi t
                  %mi log
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_{k=0}^\infty t^k \psi^k(x)
                  \= \mathrm{rank}(x) - t \frac{d}{d t} \log \lambda_{-t}(x)
          %p
            and both terms are right are additive as a function of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^k(x + y) = \psi^k(x) + \psi^k(y)
          %p
            For item 2 we can do the following calculation. Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is the class of a line bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mn 2
                  %mi L
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^2 L = 0
            hence
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi t
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{-t}(x) = 1 - t x
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %munderover
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                          %mn ∞
                        %msup
                          %mi t
                          %mi k
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtd
                        %mo =
                      %mtd
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi t
                        %mfrac
                          %mi d
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mi t
                        %mi log
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                      %mtd
                        %mo =
                      %mtd
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi t
                        %mfrac
                          %mi d
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mi t
                        %mi log
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi t
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                      %mtd
                        %mo =
                      %mtd
                        %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mi x
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mi x
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                      %mtd
                        %mo =
                      %mtd
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mi x
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                      %mtd
                        %mo =
                      %mtd
                        %munderover
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                          %mn ∞
                        %msup
                          %mi t
                          %mi k
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccl}
                  \\sum_{k=0}^\infty t^k \psi^k(x)
                  \&amp;=&amp; 1 - t \frac{d}{d t} \log \lambda_{-t}(x) \\
                  \&amp;=&amp; 1 - t \frac{d}{d t} \log(1 - t x) \\
                  \&amp;=&amp; 1 + \frac{t x}{1 - t x} \\
                  \&amp;=&amp; \frac{1}{1 - t x} \\
                  \&amp;=&amp; \sum_{k=0}^\infty t^k x^k
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            so
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_k(x) = x^k
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#basic_properties Basic properties
          #AdamsOperationOnComplexTopologicalKtheoryOfnSpheres.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (Adams operations on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+topological+K-theory"} complex topological K-theory
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+operations"} Adams operations
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+K-theory"} reduced K-theory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} 2n-sphere
              are given by:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi K
                              %mo ˜
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %msup
                                  %mi ψ
                                  %mi k
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi K
                              %mo ˜
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi k
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\widetilde K
                    \\big(
                    S^{2n}
                    \\big)
                    \&amp;
                    \\overset{ \;\;\; \psi^k\;\;\; }{\longrightarrow}
                    \&amp;
                    \\widetilde K
                    \\big(
                    S^{2n}
                    \\big)
                    \\\
                    V &amp;\mapsto&amp; k^n \cdot V
                    }
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Wirthmuller12"} Wirthmüller, Prop. on p. 45 (47 of 67)
          %h3#CompatibilityWithComplexification Compatibility with complexification
          %p
            The Adams operations are compatible with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complexification"} complexification
            map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \otimes_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{C}
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+bundles"} real vector bundles
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO-cohomology"} KO-cohomology
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU-cohomology"} KU-cohomology
