              %em Constructing and calculating Adams operations on dualisable topological modular forms
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13407"}> arXiv:2104.13407
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesInRepresentationTheory In representation theory
          %p
            Adams operations on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            of the point) are discussed in
          %ul
            %li#tomDieck79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
                , section 3.5 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Transformation+Groups+and+Representation+Theory"} Transformation Groups and Representation Theory
            %li
              %p
                Robert Boltje,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A characterization of Adams operations on representation rings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://boltje.math.ucsc.edu/publications/p01v.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dai+Tamaki"}> Dai Tamaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akira+Kono"} Akira Kono
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized Cohomology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/mmono-230"} ISBN: 978-0-8218-3514-2
            %li#tomDieck09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
                , section 6.2 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Representation theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.uni-math.gwdg.de/tammo/rep.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Boardman"}> Michael Boardman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Adams operations on Group representations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.jhu.edu/~jmb/note/adamrept.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Ehud Meir, Markus Szymik,
                %em Adams operations and symmetries of representation categories
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.03389"}> arXiv:1704.03389
                )
          %h3#in_knot_theory In knot theory
          %p
            Adams operations on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+vector+space"} modulo
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/STU+relations"} STU relations
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+operation+on+Jacobi+diagrams"}> Adams operation on Jacobi diagrams
            ) are discussed in
          %ul
            %li#BarNatan95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
              , Theorem 7, Def. 3.11 and Section 6.3.4 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the Vassiliev knot invariants
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(95)93237-2"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(95)93237-2
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.toronto.edu/drorbn/papers/OnVassiliev/OnVassiliev.pdf"} pdf
